1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,704
Meet Tuon Ta, an AI study planner built for students.

2
00:00:03,704 --> 00:00:11,502
It brings exam planning and document study into one website, helping you turn busy calendars and confusing notes into clear next steps.

3
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:14,440
The homepage introduces two tools.

4
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:20,485
Choose the study planner to organize upcoming exams, or meet the study buddy to understand your materials.

5
00:00:20,485 --> 00:00:25,819
Each tool opens in a separate tab, so you can move between planning and learning.

6
00:00:26,979 --> 00:00:29,839
In the planner, enter a subject and exam date.

7
00:00:29,839 --> 00:00:34,288
Add topics, your confidence level, and the number of hours you want to study.

8
00:00:34,288 --> 00:00:38,736
You can also click a future date directly on the calendar to select it.

9
00:00:39,896 --> 00:00:46,589
Next, choose your daily study budget, from thirty to one hundred twenty minutes, and build your plan.

10
00:00:46,589 --> 00:00:50,526
The scheduling algorithm considers deadlines, confidence, and remaining study hours.

11
00:00:50,526 --> 00:00:54,857
Sessions stay within your daily budget and finish before each exam.

12
00:00:56,017 --> 00:00:59,740
Your plan lists dates, topics, study methods, and session lengths.

13
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:05,323
Check off completed sessions to track progress, or export the plan as a CSV file.

14
00:01:05,323 --> 00:01:11,279
Exam dates and completion progress are saved in this browser, so they remain after a refresh.

15
00:01:12,439 --> 00:01:15,268
For extra support, request AI study guidance.

16
00:01:15,268 --> 00:01:20,523
It uses your exam information and available time to suggest priorities and techniques.

17
00:01:20,523 --> 00:01:26,181
The calendar schedule is controlled by code, while the AI adds explanations and coaching.

18
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:32,030
The study buddy also answers general study questions without an upload.

19
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:37,144
Ask for an explanation, a revision strategy, or help understanding a concept.

20
00:01:37,144 --> 00:01:40,128
Recent messages provide context for follow-up questions.

21
00:01:41,288 --> 00:01:49,247
To study a document, upload a PDF, Word document, text file, or Markdown file, up to ten megabytes.

22
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:52,784
You can also try the built-in biology notes.

23
00:01:52,784 --> 00:01:58,089
Text-based PDFs work directly; scanned pages need optical character recognition before uploading.

24
00:01:59,249 --> 00:02:02,196
Choose Summarize for an overview and key points.

25
00:02:02,196 --> 00:02:05,880
The response identifies its source and states the coverage used.

26
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:11,037
For longer files, selected sections are analyzed rather than every part of the document.

27
00:02:12,197 --> 00:02:17,927
Make Notes turns the material into organized revision notes, with concepts, definitions, and important ideas.

28
00:02:17,927 --> 00:02:22,894
Responses can include headings and tables to make the information easier to review.

29
00:02:24,054 --> 00:02:27,078
You can ask targeted questions about your uploaded material.

30
00:02:27,078 --> 00:02:34,471
The assistant uses the document or relevant excerpts to answer, with source labels to help you check the response against the original.

31
00:02:35,631 --> 00:02:38,554
Choose Quiz Me to generate five practice questions.

32
00:02:38,554 --> 00:02:41,112
Try answering before revealing each suggested answer.

33
00:02:41,112 --> 00:02:46,958
This turns passive reading into active recall and helps you notice topics that need another review.

34
00:02:48,118 --> 00:02:53,391
Download the conversation to keep your notes and answers, or clear the chat to start fresh.

35
00:02:53,391 --> 00:02:58,005
Files and chat stay in the current tab until you leave or clear them.

36
00:02:58,005 --> 00:03:02,290
AI responses can be inaccurate, so always compare important claims with your source.

37
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:09,041
Tuon Ta uses the open-weight GPT O S S twenty B model through Groq's hosted API.

38
00:03:09,041 --> 00:03:11,487
There is no model download for visitors.

39
00:03:11,487 --> 00:03:13,933
The API key stays on the server.

40
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:21,271
When you request AI help, selected document text and recent messages are sent to Groq, and usage follows the account's quota.

41
00:03:22,431 --> 00:03:28,457
Tuon Ta was created by Keane Prudente with OpenAI Codex assistance for design, code, and documentation.

42
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:36,367
Try the public demo, explore the source code on GitHub, and start with one subject, one question, and one small step.
